%% Invalid-guard fixture.  glp.tex Definition "Guarded Clause": a guard is a
%% conjunction of guard predicates, tests that determine clause applicability.
%% true is a body construct and not a test, so it is rejected in guard position.
%% The procedure is declared, so it is the guard that is refused and not the
%% clause of an undeclared procedure (TGLP Definition "Typed GLP Program").
procedure bad_guard(_).
bad_guard(X?) :- true | X = done.
